WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:04.820
Hi, friends!

2
00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:08.000
Let's go far, far north.

3
00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:09.300
Look!

4
00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:11.800
There is ice everywhere.

5
00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.500
The sea here is very cold.

6
00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:17.000
Brrr, so cold!

7
00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:18.980
Let's dive in.

8
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.220
We are going deep, deep down.

9
00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:25.320
It is getting dark.

10
00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:28.360
Who lives in this cold, dark sea?

11
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:31.040
Look!

12
00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:33.520
A shark is coming.

13
00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:35.920
It is a Greenland shark!

14
00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:39.160
It lives in the cold sea near Greenland.

15
00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:41.800
This shark is big.

16
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:44.440
It can grow as long as a car!

17
00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:46.980
Some grow even longer.

18
00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:49.740
Look!

19
00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:50.700
It is swimming.

20
00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:54.060
It is swimming very, very slowly.

21
00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:56.820
It is slower than you can walk.

22
00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:00.300
Its tail is going swish, swish.

23
00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:03.620
Look at its eyes.

24
00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:07.240
Many have a tiny animal hanging on one eye!

25
00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:10.020
It looks like a little white string.

26
00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:12.920
So it may not see very well.

27
00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:17.300
But it finds food with a super nose.

28
00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:19.420
Sniff, sniff!

29
00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:22.520
It eats fish.

30
00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:24.600
It even eats seals!

31
00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:28.220
It also eats leftovers on the sea floor.

32
00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:31.780
Now, here is a big surprise.

33
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.600
This shark can get very, very old.

34
00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:38.280
It can live for hundreds of years!

35
00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.520
Some may be 400 years old.

36
00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:45.060
That is older than your great-great-great-grandma!

37
00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:48.160
Let's say the words.

38
00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:50.220
Greenland shark.

39
00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:53.500
Ice.

40
00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:56.930
Cold.

41
00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:00.050
Deep.

42
00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:03.300
Dark.

43
00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:06.600
Big.

44
00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:10.020
Swim.

45
00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:13.480
Slow.

46
00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:16.780
Eyes.

47
00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:20.200
Nose.

48
00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:23.600
Fish.

49
00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:27.000
Seal.

50
00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:30.200
Old.

51
00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:33.540
Great job!

52
00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:37.200
Bye-bye, Greenland shark!

53
00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:40.320
It is swimming away, very slowly.

54
00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:42.940
Oh, it is still here!

55
00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:44.860
It is so slow!

56
00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:47.200
See you next time!
